cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these data, please cite the article listed under references."
title: "stclq: scalable permutation inference for spatio-temporal co-location quotients"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of the spatio-temporal co-location quotient (STCLQ) with
  global and local variants, four permutation nulls, bandwidth selection and
  diagnostics, together with the experiment drivers, results, figures and manuscript
  sources of the accompanying paper. The permutation engine builds the spatial
  neighbourhood structure once and reuses it, so a single permutation costs one sparse
  matrix-matrix product rather than a traversal of all N^2 ordered pairs.
